## Status

Accepted. `cloud-itonami-isic-3012` implemented as a fresh
from-scratch actor repository under the `cloud-itonami` org and
promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry`
registry, following the verified fresh-scaffold + mandatory-
verification protocol used across this fleet's careful,
smaller-batch rollout (after the prior 18-agent haiku batch's 61%
defect rate, 96+ consecutive agents on the stricter protocol —
capable model + mandatory `clojure -M:test` verification — have all
succeeded; this is the next one).

## Context

`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry entry `{:id \"3012\" ...}` carries
`:name \"Building of pleasure and sporting boats\"` (ISIC Rev.5 3012) —
verified against a fresh clone of `kotoba-lang/industry` before any
implementation work began, per this fleet's mandatory ID/name-match
discipline (multiple prior agents in this fleet have mislabeled their
assigned ISIC class; this run confirmed the live `:name` matches the
assigned scope before writing anything). `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/
cloud-itonami-isic-3012` 404'd before this repo was created —
confirmed fresh scaffold, no prior repo to adopt or merge into. The
registry's pre-existing `:repo` value was the legacy placeholder
`https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C3012` (never created —
the standard \"spec, not yet implemented\" placeholder pattern this
fleet uses fleet-wide), not a real repo to migrate from.

The reference architecture mirrored closely is `cloud-itonami-isic-3092`
(Manufacture of bicycles and invalid carriages, 77 tests / 215
assertions in that repo) — the closest architectural analog: both are
back-office coordination actors for a fixed manufacturing plant
producing recreational/sporting vehicles with a real physical safety
dimension, sharing the same four-op shape (`:log-production-batch`/
`:schedule-maintenance`/`:flag-safety-concern`/`:coordinate-shipment`)
and the same two-entity verified/registered gate structure. 3012's own
hazard AND certification-regime profile is distinct from 3092's:
hull-molding/lamination, rigging, final-assembly and water-test
(buoyancy/stability) inspection (rather than 3092's frame-weld/test-
bench-only inspection), a `:product-category` closed set spanning
sailboat/motorboat/inflatable-boat/yacht/catamaran/personal-
watercraft/sport-fishing-boat/canoe/kayak/skiff/rowing-boat, a
`:hull-length-m` plausibility check (0-100, spanning small kayaks/
skiffs through large pleasure/sporting motor and sailing yachts, still
distinct from ISIC 3011's larger commercial/naval ship hulls) in place
of 3092's `:weight-capacity-kg` (0-300), and a permanent ISO 12217
(stability and buoyancy assessment) / CE Recreational Craft Directive
(2013/53/EU) marine-classification-certification-authority block in
place of 3092's ISO 4210/ISO 7176 block. The full domain adaptation
(equipment/product vocabulary, hazard language) is recorded in the
child repo's own `docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`.

## Decision

### Decision 1: Scope — a boat-building-plant PLANT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, not hull-molding/assembly-line control authority, NOT a marine-classification authority

`cloud-itonami-isic-3012` is `BoatAdvisor ⊣ Boat Building Plant
Operations Governor`, a langgraph-clj StateGraph with an append-only
audit ledger (same pattern as every actor in this fleet — see skill
`build-actor`). Closed allowlist of four ops, all `:effect :propose`
only:
- `:log-production-batch` — hull-molding/rigging/assembly batch, output-quality/test-result data logging
- `:schedule-maintenance` — hull-molding/rigging/final-assembly/water-test-equipment maintenance scheduling proposal
- `:flag-safety-concern` — surface a hull-integrity-defect/buoyancy-test-failure/materials-safety concern, ALWAYS escalates
- `:coordinate-shipment` — outbound product shipment coordination

### Decision 2: HARD invariants (no override)

1. Plant/batch record (equipment for maintenance, batch for shipment) must be independently verified/registered before any action.
2. `:effect` must be `:propose` only (never a direct-write bypass).
3. Any proposal touching hull-molding/rigging/final-assembly/water-test-equipment control or a marine-classification/seaworthiness-certification-authority decision (e.g. ISO 12217 / CE Recreational Craft Directive) is a hard, permanent block.
4. The op allowlist is closed — the four ops above only.

Elaborated into twelve concrete governor checks (propose-only effect,
closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist, permanent
equipment-actuate block, permanent marine-classification-authority
block, independent equipment verification before maintenance
scheduling, double-schedule guard, independent batch verification
before shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute,
product-category validation, hull-length plausibility validation,
hull-defect-rate plausibility validation) — see child repo README/ADR
for the full enumeration.

### Decision 3: ESCALATE — always human sign-off

`:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor,
regardless of confidence — never auto-decided, no threshold below
escalation. Low-confidence proposals also escalate (SOFT, human may
approve). `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to
auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean (no physical/
financial risk in a production-batch data-logging patch).

### Decision 4: cljs-first / portable — no JVM interop

All source is `.cljc`, invoked exclusively via `langgraph.graph/run*`
(not `.invoke`, which is not cljs-portable), per this repository's
mandatory `.cljc`/`.kotoba` runtime priority (kotoba wasm →
clojurewasm → ClojureScript → nbb, JVM/bb downgraded to compat-layer
status). No JVM-only interop anywhere in `src/` or `test/`.

## Consequences

(+) ISIC 3012 (Building of pleasure and sporting boats) now has a
governed, auditable, forkable OSS plant-operations coordination actor
with an explicit, structural, permanently unconditional block against
ever self-issuing an ISO 12217/CE Recreational Craft Directive
marine-classification certification — a regulatory-authority boundary
distinct from the prior bicycle/wheelchair actor's ISO 4210/ISO 7176
boundary and the motorcycle actor's ECE R78/ECE R40 boundary.

(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry entry `3012` promoted from
`:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` corrected from
the legacy `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C3012` placeholder naming to the
`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3012` convention used by every other
`:implemented` entry in this fleet (e.g. 3091, 3092, 2211).

(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer — no integration with real
plant-management databases (equipment telemetry, batch tracking,
freight dispatch, or an authoritative classification-society
database). Equipment actuation and hull-molding/rigging/assembly-line
operation remain human-controlled via external channels, and marine
classification/seaworthiness certification remains a regulatory-
authority process entirely outside this actor, as intended.

